  "interpretation": "Generic three-handler rejected Update can return a representative when assumed directly at the request script. Actual naming retirement instead places it in a distinct custody script. The new same-context control requires all three current handlers to accept and then the actual custody handler to refuse zero-burn redirection; a custody-only exact-burn positive controls that refusal. These are synthetic validator-context tests, not ledger inclusion or reachable naming setup, and the burn positive does not execute the representative mint policy.",
